    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0464" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2429</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-25T11:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 25, 1916, 11 a. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 26, 2.10 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3528. Learn on good authority that Foreign Office here was informed that Baron
                    Zwiedinek, Austro-Hungarian Chargé d’Affaires, had cabled his Government prior
                    to issue of German memorandum about armed merchant vessels that you personally
                    had informed him that declaration of that nature from Central powers would be
                    welcomed by you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
